Rule 20 (channel dimension must be broadcast-compatible when both inputs are 4D tensors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 4 then shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_2, 1) ∨ shape(v_1, 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, 1) = 1
>>
Rule 21 (1D tensors must have matching lengths or one must have length 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0) ∨ shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, 0) = 1
>>
Rule 22 (trailing dimension must be broadcast-compatible when inputs are 3D and 2D tensors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 3 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 2 then shape(v_1, 2) = shape(v_2, 1) ∨ shape(v_1, 2) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, 1) = 1
